# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# THE BUG THIS FIXES (reported from production, Aug 2026):
#   Navigating inside the app worked. Pasting a URL like /knowledge into
#   the address bar, opening a link to it from outside, or refreshing the
#   page returned 404.
#
# WHY IT HAPPENED:
#   This is a client-side-routed app (jaspr_router). Routes like
#   /knowledge or /bots/42 exist ONLY in the browser after main.dart.js
#   has loaded — there is no file at web/knowledge on disk. In-app
#   navigation never asks the server for that path, so it always worked.
#   A direct hit, a refresh, or an external link DOES ask the server,
#   which looks for a file that isn't there and correctly returns 404.
#
# THE FIX:
#   Serve index.html for any path that isn't a real file, with HTTP 200
#   (NOT a 301/302 — the URL must stay as typed so the router can read it
#   and show the right page). index.html boots the app, the router reads
#   window.location, and the correct page renders.
#
# WHY THIS DOESN'T BREAK ASSETS:
#   Cloudflare Pages checks for an actual file on disk BEFORE applying
#   these rules. main.dart.js, styles.css and every image resolve
#   normally; only paths with no matching file fall through to here.
#
# WHY 200 AND NOT 404-WITH-index.html:
#   A 404 status would tell crawlers and link previews the page doesn't
#   exist even though it renders fine, and some clients refuse to run
#   scripts on error responses.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

